                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr. Conger.</hi></head>
                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Telegram—Paraphrase.]</seg></opener>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1900-10-22"><hi rendition="#italic">October 22,
                        1900</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>(Mr. Hay states that he has learned, through the Italian ambassador, of Li’s
                    assurance of the Emperor’s early return to Pekin, and suggesting the return of
                    the summer palace, which is favored by ministers of Italy and Austria. Any step
                    which would tend to reinstate the Imperial authority and afford guaranty for the
                    negotiation and execution of an effective settlement would be welcomed by the
                    Government of the United States.)</p>
            </div>
        </body>
